  "experiment": "In a four-position Flash Next verify wave, four existing readers each claim a full expert and read its missing up, gate and down projections as one validated batch. The three GGUF ranges still use separate positioned reads. The queue signals availability on completion of the expert. Admission, leases, read error latch, worker drain and routed arithmetic come from the existing demand queue. Optional probe for 8 GiB; tiled prefill is unchanged.",
  "protocol": "Same binary per pair, fresh isolated Metal server per run. Same eight-ID warmup, uncached 912-ID request, compact DFlash2 depth 3, 64 real greedy outputs, no kernel or phase profiling in A-B-B-A. A uses the previous reader and B enables FLASH_VERIFY_WHOLE_EXPERT=1. Rates count 63 first-to-last stream intervals. Aggregate TPS uses pooled time. File cache and thermal state are uncontrolled. Separate diagnostic processes ran with the expert-counter probe from atomic-engine-flash-next-dflash3-rounds-8gib.json to confirm target shape and measure expert readiness in 24 four-position verify graphs.",
